o-liquid-chunk-end{%- endcomment -%}</div><div data-rid="3a537419-c620-42a0-b789-f309d93c7730" class="r-15y5s2k"><div data-rid="db58f0b3-1275-431d-b9b5-bfc77aa541b0" class="r-5oyy1a alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Frequently Asked Questions</p></span></div><div data-rid="72aba559-f948-45c4-9faa-d5b70b98f04b" class="r-1byr88x" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="cb03d5f3-0201-4327-8098-0b54fbf8ade6" class="r-ni3zuv" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="74beffd7-65d5-49c9-86fd-763ac18111c8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R1jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1aq8c1e"><div data-rid="bd5d1f6d-74d6-4050-8b30-5107fb96ceb9" class="r-mklmey alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What is monthlies?</p></span></div><div data-rid="43200c0e-bc5b-46c0-8a92-ff87fa993adb" class="r-df5ju3"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R1jr2:"><div data-rid="910786a8-8979-440d-872e-93e2a6ce0f4e" class="r-b14f9v"><div data-rid="9879578f-edad-4856-891c-6cfcc476ff6b" class="r-ev7xft alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Monthlies is a premium supplement that combines natural ingredients to support your menstrual cycle. You simply add one scoop to water once a day.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="88a7bceb-4717-4c13-9eb0-cb20437e9f79" class="r-1t1ca3e" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="8fb3f729-2eca-4e0e-a5d9-80b5e0cdc01e" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R2jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-v0qls6"><div data-rid="28be3280-5978-4507-b804-ec0eb5a0eac2" class="r-i1j4cz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What does monthlies taste like?</p></span></div><div data-rid="7ec266f2-2b3e-4a73-8ea4-c46b32e200ce" class="r-xhdvye"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R2jr2:"><div data-rid="93057631-aaea-44a2-a447-005c4b8c42ad" class="r-1nfzx0n"><div data-rid="6c7c5d9c-24d0-4490-89f0-fd2c19078022" class="r-1fw5bqa alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies has a tropical, slightly gingery taste. If it's a bit strong for you, you can try mixing it with more water and sipping it slowly. You can also add it to a smoothie or blend it into a cold beverage to make it easier and more enjoyable to take daily.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="c923ff71-f703-4ca4-a13e-fb612739bb5b" class="r-eamv48" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="b5a0eae3-d554-4c40-a2fa-29e287a642cf" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R3jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-10hzker"><div data-rid="659167d0-7da7-4a95-b029-436fcb625a9e" class="r-1lnxued alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I'm using hormonal contraceptive?</p></span></div><div data-rid="1c9677be-4208-4a7f-bbf1-23978d5e9a6c" class="r-q848c6"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R3jr2:"><div data-rid="b59db4a2-e7be-43c4-a5c7-1dbca0af335f" class="r-12a003n"><div data-rid="dbcafab2-ce3b-47cc-8324-8a1e3b072940" class="r-q0y62e alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You can take monthlies while on birth control or hormonal contraceptive pills; however, it's essential to understand that the effectiveness of monthlies may vary since your hormones are already being regulated. Additionally, monthlies could potentially interact with your hormonal birth control. To ensure safety, it's always best to consult your doctor before adding any new supplements to your routine. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="5a5dd9d9-402f-42ee-be7b-fac3fa283fe3" class="r-4h7jiq" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="2528d010-0011-40e1-aca9-9c2a46cab235" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R4jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-6bo0lm"><div data-rid="4e8bbbb6-7270-4cb6-b941-c6440aeb57db" class="r-c4j9h7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is monthlies suitable for a teenager?</p></span></div><div data-rid="a06abb19-bc7b-47ef-a72a-0d85a0d6cfa9" class="r-rx38mc"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R4jr2:"><div data-rid="0be8f02c-ab46-4ced-945c-fb999a1eec9e" class="r-hdof3k"><div data-rid="85a5cfdb-4c53-4977-92e5-60f33daf5469" class="r-18z57je alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies is recommended for females above the age of 16, as this is when their menstrual cycle and hormonal system usually begins to stabilise. For teenagers under the age of 16 (18 in Germany), we suggest consulting a doctor before introducing any new supplement. While monthlies is formulated with science-backed vitamins, minerals and plant extracts that support menstrual health, it's always best to get individual advice for the teen's unique needs. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="40a5290b-c5f9-46ec-8a57-d7d257fc77db" class="r-1kjx8e3" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="a33bf29c-d686-4df2-a251-fb986884bfca" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R5jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-13hljbn"><div data-rid="c1692fc9-3f51-4435-a0fe-4b31ea2d87d6" class="r-jg9zjp alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have endometriosis?</p></span></div><div data-rid="c53d26d3-5dd3-46b8-b901-8e5d8b4ea80d" class="r-d5uz09"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R5jr2:"><div data-rid="0b8a06ed-f976-4be2-936c-7d823ca65758" class="r-pf39fb"><div data-rid="047667cc-c7f6-4556-8ba8-ad629dbf68e2" class="r-9cjgc4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have endometriosis. While monthlies is not a treatment for endometriosis, it's designed to support menstrual well-being by addressing some of the underlying triggers of period pain, such a hormonal imbalances, prostaglandin overproduction and nutrient gaps. However, we always recommend you to check with your doctors before adding any new supplements to your routine and check for possible interactions with medications. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="914d468a-0ff4-4526-b15f-02da9a561248" class="r-pits7v" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="1a139bed-bf37-43ec-89c0-f0d8b7537c77" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R6jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-4yay40"><div data-rid="d34ad4c3-46b2-4a3d-8986-a90ee31ecaa7" class="r-177remx alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have IBS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="b9a0f274-3f15-4625-b105-ebb4c87bcb4e" class="r-13f6vv4"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R6jr2:"><div data-rid="e7bd3d7d-e664-4ecb-8f5b-47e22651a381" class="r-f7fqsq"><div data-rid="83d71978-966e-434c-9256-d8ebcf9a94eb" class="r-17620dc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>monthlies can be taken by those with IBS, but since IBS can involve sensitivities to certain ingredients, we recommend reviewing our full ingredient list before introducing it to your routine. If you're unsure about how your body might react, especially to certain dosages and ingredients, it's best to speak to your doctor or a health care professional who understands your condition. </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="b6a2dc07-fe6c-413f-b246-bcb92420fac2" class="r-1ghjmp2" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="8233fb36-d83c-4ffa-8ceb-d3f42d13486b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R7jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1g2k96z"><div data-rid="f9dea94b-cdf5-4394-a7f8-beb581dbec34" class="r-1mek5pf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I have PCOS?</p></span></div><div data-rid="9ccedc1b-58e1-4f28-a309-976ec2a22124" class="r-6ty43x"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: 100%" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div><div hidden="" id="replo-:R7jr2:"><div data-rid="20c75404-7431-4e9d-a541-eb4544e48368" class="r-n960fp"><div data-rid="5ae55465-6358-457e-95b3-892b6a77da30" class="r-1bvc8yq alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have PCOS, as there are many ingredients that may benefit those with PCOS.</p><br><p>However, monthlies is not meant to treat any medical condition so you should always check with your doctor before incorporating new supplements into your routine. Please also check possible interactions with your medications (if any). </p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="16834ebc-d475-4d67-80d4-69d2edb68bb1" class="r-17e6es9" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="4f8ff77b-eed4-45a1-9bdf-4f8913e34969" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R8jr2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-cq18kf"><div data-rid="4a13995e-4310-40f8-9b3f-eea1683460e3" class="r-4w1uq7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can I take monthlies if I am breastfeeding or pregnant?</p></span></div><div data-rid="f811466f-13ee-44f1-8b97-f5a3ffc6e6cc" class="r-eudu0j"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24